        "like": 12
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "last time I checked, this was a sandbox game that advertises the ability to be creative. The few people who feel entitled to create a business in a sandbox game are the problem.\n\nAny person I come across who is wearing an avatar of mine without paying, gets a free coupon so they can receive updates. In the rare chance that I see someone in a screwed up ripped version of my personal avatar, I'll help them, teach them, or make them something cooler. More chances to be creative. Why would I shit on someone who clearly liked what I made?\n\n I don't think making the game worse, so we can protect IP is the right choice. We were all creative in this game before anyone had the idea to start selling their work.  \n\nThis canny post is all over the place, how is this even being tracked when it states multiple problems? FYI you don't need an exploit to download a vrca, it's already on your computer, unencrypted, because that's what is best for the rest of us who are busy being social in a social sandbox game. \n\nFor real go play the Facebook VR game if you want this. It is completely sterile. If you are scared to go to a public world because someone might \"steal\" (copy) your personal avatar, get a life.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
